g":0.33,"qtext":"<p>Consider the combinational circuit shown below:</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/49320ea0af70d688d62ec0239bdc141e8e76d3c2.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div>With <em>W</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>W</em><sub>2</sub> as inputs, the given circuit implements a</div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> EX-OR logic</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> EX-NOR logic</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> OR-logic</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> NOR logic</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/d27e203f1de5cec66952750e1c56d0c38c64bb17.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":6,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>Which of the following is not an application of a gray code?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> It is used in transmission of digital signal.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> It is generally used in angle measurement devices.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> It is generally used for arithmetic operation.</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> It is generally used as a position indicator.</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(c)<br />\n&bull; Gray Code is a binary code where two successive values differ in only one bit. It is used in<br />\ntransmission of digital signal as it reduces occurrence of error.<br />\n&bull; The cyclic property of gray code makes it useful for angle measurement.<br />\n&bull; It is generally used as a position indicator as two successive values differ in only one bit.<br />\n&bull; Gray code does not use positional weighting, making it unsuitable for arithmetic operations.</p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":7,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>The below figure shows the output of a transistor level circuit connected to the select line of a 2-input multiplexer.</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/e3fabe49b13b0fe2b4caa7e4d89900c3288ab350.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div>The minterms present in the output logic function <em>F</em> are</div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> Σ<em>m</em>(1, 2, 4, 7)</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> Σ<em>m</em>(1, 4, 5, 7)</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> Σ<em>m</em>(3, 5, 6, 7)</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> Σ<em>m</em>(0, 3, 6, 7)</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/6d867759678a3a989f641d4ac4c79f49995ddec8.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>\n<div> </div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":8,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>A n-bit ADC has following specifications: 16-bit counter, clock rate = 4 MHz, input voltage = 12 V and capacitor = 0.47 μF.<br />\nIf the maximum integrator output voltage is –7 V when the counter have cycled through 2<sup>n</sup> counts, then the value of resistor in the integrator is _______ × 10<sup>3</sup> Ω. (upto two decimal places)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"59.74","high":"59.74"},"solution":"<p>59.74 (57.00 - 61.00)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/0170418e18ea4cf17745a0f3de0263fe2a80c1e8.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":9,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>The number of self-dual functions possible with ‘<em>n</em>’ Boolean variables is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 2<em><sup>n</sup></em></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 2<sup><em>n</em> –1</sup></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/7bc5e4f3262e4d565ac7fd733090a7c0eba731fc.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/30ce8a5262aedf04fa69313ef5015bd85556d0a1