uency is _________ MHz. (upto one decimal place)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"22.2","high":"22.2"},"solution":"<p>22.2 (21.0 - 23.0)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/d9b8cb4f906c43bcefe2429e7efcb6a67e093340.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":18,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>Consider the MUX circuit shown in the figure below.</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/68b1f9264398e0cf0f2bff8c4bb077d4797365c7.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>\n<div>The counter is a 2 bit up counter which is initially set to ‘00’ at ‘<em>t</em><sub>0</sub>’ time.<br />\nThe clock is applied to the counter which in turn is used to drive a 4 × 1 MUX and a 1 × 4 DEMUX<br />\ncircuit, then the time at which the output <img src=\"/media/0183e0b018c75e52cfdb081e4775ccae42ae3f02.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> will occur for the first time and its value is respectively given by<br />\n(Assume the circuits have zero delay and <em>t<sub>n</sub></em> represents the <em>n</em><sup>th</sup> clock pulse)</div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/a4964fce58ff872741b82ab73c2c4f7f7b3a66bc.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/cd96641075a2629edc24836495806a93d396105b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/361f762ef5326324393ea858aed41c2ac6d424d5.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/3f00cb3010276b75bfdae13d462d4096d4c201de.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/24119571b0f169214839c5a1abf1adcc18096f6b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":19,"type":"MSQ","correct":"C,D","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Consider the circuit shown below:</p>\n<d